// TEST: Range SymIdx Tagged Slot Warns
// The tag side of `range<SymIdx<...>>`, and the WARNING half of the pair whose
// ERROR half is 175.
//
// `range<LatIdx>` flows LatIdx's tag onto the kernel's index param, which is
// what makes `A(i)` typecheck with no annotation
// (TypeCheck.elemTypeForIterationIndex). A multi-rank slot gets no such tag:
// the params come out plain Int64, so every read of the I3-tagged array `v` is
// an untagged-integer index -- BL4003 as a WARNING, twice (v(p0) and
// v(p0 + p1)), and the program compiles and runs to 172's values.
//
// Name that same SymIdx group and the identical program HARD-ERRORS instead
// (175). Nothing semantic separates the two spellings.
//
// The group here is deliberately anonymous on BOTH counts -- no alias AND a
// literal extent. `range<SymIdx<2, I3>>`, naming only the COMPONENT, is a
// third behaviour again: it typechecks with these same two warnings and then
// fails to compile, emitting `S_extents[0] = __range0.extents[0];` for an
// `__range0` that was never declared. That is a codegen defect, not a
// refusal, so it has no honest pin here; see docs/formalism.md 7.3.
type I3 = Idx<3>
let v: Array<Float like I3> = [2.0, 3.0, 5.0]
let sym = method_for(range<SymIdx<2, 3>>) <@> lambda(p0, p1) -> v(p0) * v(p0 + p1) |> compute
// WARN: BL4003  (untagged index into an I3-tagged slot)
// EXPECT: sym = [[4, 6, 10], [9, 15], [25]]
